    native_primitive_to_i64_ufcs_collision_2026-07-24, 1, "2026-11-10 fix lane: premise re-verified on release/1.0.0 -- MethodResolver.try_ufcs (src/compiler/35.semantics/resolve_strategies.spl) resolved x.to_i64()/to_f64()/to_text()/len() on an i64/f64/text receiver to ANY same-named free function in scope (exact-typed or Infer first param; src/lib/common/complex defines a real fn to_f64(n: i64)), so native lowering dispatched the primitive intrinsic to the free fn. MIR-level recovery (try_lower_unresolved_ufcs_v1) already guards by nominal owner; the hole was the semantic resolver. Fix: primitive_intrinsic_method_name_v1 predicate; try_ufcs declines primitive-receiver intrinsic names (primitive wins over UFCS; instance/trait owners keep priority). Specs: test/01_unit/compiler/35.semantics/primitive_receiver_intrinsic_ufcs_precedence_spec.spl (red 1/6 passed -> green 6/6; covers to_i64 on i64/f64/text, siblings to_f64/to_text/len, and a non-intrinsic UFCS name still resolving), test/01_unit/lib/primitive_conversion_ufcs_precedence_spec.spl (interpreter parity, 4/4). Native-build verification of test/03_system/native/primitive_to_i64_collision.spl still pending (no native builds in this lane)."

